    "result_text": "All green. The full build succeeds \u2014 `AcceptanceTest` is the only test class in the project (the other files under `acceptance/` are support classes).\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `riskFlag` field on the owner response following the codebase's existing pattern of small, self-contained `@Aspect` response-advice classes.\n\n**Two files touched, no large class edited:**\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added the read-only `riskFlag` boolean to the `Owner` schema (defaults to `false`), which regenerates `OwnerDto` with a `setRiskFlag`.\n\n2. **`.../rest/advice/OwnerRiskFlagAdvice.java`** (new) \u2014 a focused aspect that sets `riskFlag` on `getOwner`/`addOwner` responses to `true` when **any** of the three spec signals hold:\n   - **possible duplicate** \u2014 a live (non-deleted) owner shares this owner's last name and postcode but has a different telephone (matching the existing `possibleDuplicate` definition in the schema);\n   - **disposable-adjacent email** \u2014 the email domain is, or is a subdomain of, a known disposable-mail provider (the same blocklist the disposable-email validator uses; exact matches are rejected at creation, so stored ones are the \"adjacent\" subdomains);\n   - **over soft capacity** \u2014 the owner's city already holds \u2265 40 owners (the soft threshold below the hard cap of 50 enforced elsewhere), using the same case/whitespace-insensitive city normalization as the capacity aspects.\n\n**Structural-impact choices:** the new logic lives entirely in one new, cohesive class \u2014 so the surrounding complexity (`WMC_other`) I had to reason about is just its own small helpers, not the large `Owner`, mapper, or service classes. I did not modify any existing method, so no existing function's complexity or line count was disturbed; each new predicate is a short single-purpose method.\n\nTest result: `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` \u2014 `BUILD SUCCESS`.",
